  "text_blocks": {
    "source-3-0": "Measurement Module #2 – Digital Audio Effects",
    "source-3-1": "Teaching Assistant | Yonsei University | Fall 2024, 2025, 2026",
    "source-1-0": "Welcome to my musical journey!",
    "source-1-1": "Here are some moments from my years in music, including live performances, experiments with sound, and everything in between.",
    "source-1-2": "I hope you enjoy looking around!",
    "source-21-0": "Here are some moments from my live performances over the years, from my early days in bands to more recent shows.",
    "source-21-1": "These photos capture the stages I've performed on, the musicians I've played with, and the memories I've made along the way.",
    "source-19-0": "CTAG-FX grew out of my interest in exploring and shaping guitar tones through audio effects. It uses AI to interpret text prompts and generate synthesizer parameter configurations, which are then reinterpreted as controls for a tone-shaping audio FX processor.",
    "source-19-1": "This video demonstrates how the resulting audio effects can be used in actual guitar performance.",
    "source-19-2": "For more details about the research, please visit the project page below.",
    "source-19-3": "CTAG-FX — Full Project Details",
    "source-4-0": "As a teaching assistant, I introduced students to the engineering principles behind audio effects through hands-on demonstrations.",
    "source-4-1": "I conducted in-person laboratory instruction in Fall 2024 and provided video-based demonstrations in Fall 2025 and 2026.",
    "source-9-0": "This video introduces various guitar effects, including wah, overdrive, compression, distortion, fuzz, delay, reverb, and flanger, combining technical explanations with live guitar demonstrations.",
    "source-10-0": "Original Korean-language video",
    "source-16-0": "Live guitar demonstration at Yonsei University (Fall 2024)",
    "source-23-0": "When I Was in Middle School...☺️"
  },
